{title: All People That on Earth Do Dwell}
{artist: William Kethe / Louis Bourgeois}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: all-people-that-on-earth-do-dwell.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (All_People_That_On_Earth_Do_Dwell-Old_100th) and the Cyber Hymnal score (88% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]All peo[D]ple [Em]that [Bm]on [Em]earth [D]do [G]dwell,
[G]Sing to the [D7]Lord [Em]with [C]cheer[G]ful [D]voice.
[Em]Him [D]serve [G]with [D]fear, His [C]praise [D]forth [G]tell;
[G]Come ye [Em]be[D]fore [Am]Him and [D7]re[G]joice.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]The Lord, [D]ye [Em]know, [Bm]is [Em]God [D]in[G]deed;
[G]Without our [D7]aid [Em]He [C]did [G]us [D]make;
[Em]We [D]are [G]His [D]folk, He [C]doth [D]us [G]feed,
[G]And for [Em]His [D]sheep [Am]He doth [D7]us [G]take.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O en[D]ter [Em]then [Bm]His [Em]gates [D]with [G]praise;
[G]Approach with [D7]joy [Em]His [C]courts [G]un[D]to;
[Em]Praise, [D]laud, [G]and [D]bless His [C]name [D]al[G]ways,
[G]For it [Em]is [D]seem[Am]ly so [D7]to [G]do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]For why? [D]The [Em]Lord [Bm]our [Em]God [D]is [G]good,
[G]His mercy [D7]is [Em]for[C]ev[G]er [D]sure:
[Em]His [D]truth [G]at [D]all times [C]firm[D]ly [G]stood,
[G]And shall [Em]from [D]age [Am]to age [D7]en[G]dure.
{end_of_verse}
